 "_comment": "Hoenn & Seek (part 20a): overworld Pokémon, as HnS has in Johto and Kanto. tools/hoenn/gen_hoenn_ow_mons.py adds them to each kept Hoenn map's map.json (script HoennSeek_EventScript_OWMon marks them; re-runs replace them). Maps with a wild table get mons drawn from it (land table on grass/floor, surf table on water), split by FLAG_DAY_POKEMON / FLAG_NIGHT_POKEMON where the map has a _Night table. 'towns' lists ambient mons for maps without encounters (or adds to them): [species, count, where] with where = land | water | day | night | water_night. 'no_land' skips a map's land table (Route 130's is Mirage Island's); 'never_species' are left out (Kecleon is meant to be invisible).",
